// PlayerModelLib resolves attribute descriptions by first checking for a
// value-suffixed key "charattribute-{attr}-{value}", then falling back to
// "charattribute-{attr}" as a format string filled with the value.
// Non-suffixed format strings are the maintainable form and are what this
// file uses. Value-suffixed literals are a trap: they break silently when
// a trait value changes.
